Package: bhfvar
Title: Bayesian Hybrid Framework for Variance Decomposition in Complex Surveys
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: 
    person("JoonHo", "Lee", email = "jlee296@ua.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Implements the Bayesian pseudo-likelihood framework for variance
    decomposition in complex surveys with post-hoc domains described in Lee and
    Hooper (2026) <doi:10.3390/math14030512>. Domain and stratum effects are
    crossed, primary sampling units are nested within strata, and domain and
    PSU effects carry the centering constraints given in the article. Estimands
    A, A*, and B are computed on the probability scale with explicit provenance
    and diagnostics. Posterior intervals are pseudo-posterior credible
    intervals. In a reduced balanced synthetic study, pooled primary 90 percent
    coverage was 0.900 (cluster interval 0.871 to 0.928), but coverage is not
    guaranteed for other designs or every tested condition.
